Publish the PCM's apparent surface charges as named component results.

moist hands the host the potential adjoint w_phi = dE/dphi.  For a stationary
model (C-PCM, COSMO) that is the apparent surface charge q; for IEF-PCM, SS(V)PE
and the other non-symmetric models it is the symmetrized adjoint qsym, not q.
Both are held by the component but only its energy was readable.  This adds a
list_fields hook to the component type (no fields by default), through which a
PCM component publishes q and a layer component (IEF-PCM, SS(V)PE, LPB, ...) q
and qsym: SolvationModel.components[i].get("q") after an evaluation.  Nothing
existing changes.

